{
  "description": "Whether an issue_comment event's comment is a maintainer's. A maintainer is a GitHub account of type User whose GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/collaborators/{login}/permission answers 200 with permission admin or write (maintain reads as write, triage as read). The comment's author and its last writer must both be maintainers: a created comment's writer is the sender; an edited comment's is the sender only when changes names the body; any other action writes nothing. A comment made through a GitHub App (performed_via_github_app) is never a maintainer's. The author is read before the writer, each wholly (a non-User account is \"not\" without a read) before the next, and the first \"not\" or unavailable read decides; a login is read once, compared without case. permissions maps a login to its permission, to the HTTP status GitHub answers, or to null when the connection fails; a login not listed answers 404. 403, 429, 5xx and a failed connection are unavailable: the caller fails closed and may retry. Any other status is \"not\". A missing sender is \"not\". The backend (packages/backend/internal/services/github_maintainer_comment_vectors_test.go) runs these vectors.",
